264
00:18:02,750 --> 00:18:04,500
-Have the prince taken to his chambers,
-What?

265
00:18:04,583 --> 00:18:05,416
If you would.

266
00:18:07,333 --> 00:18:08,458
My young master,

267
00:18:08,958 --> 00:18:10,958
Eh… would you come with me?

268
00:18:11,041 --> 00:18:13,208
Mh. Mh… Oh…

269
00:18:15,916 --> 00:18:16,750
Here, dad.

270
00:18:18,958 --> 00:18:19,958
Mhh… Oh…

271
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:22,208
-Hey…
-Do as I say, son.

272
00:18:24,916 --> 00:18:26,875
Uh… Hm.

273
00:18:27,708 --> 00:18:28,541
Huh?

274
00:18:47,041 --> 00:18:47,875
Uh…

275
00:18:53,750 --> 00:18:56,375
Uh… Uh… no, wait! Procustes…

276
00:18:57,583 --> 00:18:59,250
Yes… Your Highness?

277
00:18:59,750 --> 00:19:01,458
What's wrong with my parents?

278
00:19:01,541 --> 00:19:02,666
Well, uhm…

279
00:19:02,750 --> 00:19:03,791
you see…

280
00:19:04,458 --> 00:19:08,250
a heavy burden rests upon the
shoulders of the King and Queen, my Lord.

281
00:19:08,750 --> 00:19:10,250
Our kind grows weaker.

282
00:19:10,333 --> 00:19:12,291
Its strength, its vigor, its presence,

283
00:19:12,375 --> 00:19:13,541
all slipping away,

284
00:19:13,625 --> 00:19:15,583
because of the human scum.

285
00:19:16,083 --> 00:19:17,666
-Your parents are the first ones to
-Ow…

286
00:19:17,750 --> 00:19:19,458
feel it, and the kingdom follows.

287
00:19:19,541 --> 00:19:20,875
No, I won't allow it!

288
00:19:20,958 --> 00:19:22,041
I'm going to help them

289
00:19:22,125 --> 00:19:23,375
Oh, I really wish you could, but…

290
00:19:23,458 --> 00:19:24,291
Huh?

291
00:19:24,375 --> 00:19:26,500
I'm afraid it's out of your hands, my
Lord.

292
00:19:26,583 --> 00:19:27,958
-But once they're gone,
-Uhm…

293
00:19:28,041 --> 00:19:30,416
-Eh, eh…
-you and I shall work together as one.

294
00:19:30,916 --> 00:19:33,500
I will share my masterpieces so that
you may send them to humankind

295
00:19:33,583 --> 00:19:34,916
in the form of horrific nightmares.

296
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,708
Hm… Ow…

297
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:40,125
Unfortunately we live at the mercy

298
00:19:40,208 --> 00:19:41,583
of those simple and

299
00:19:41,666 --> 00:19:42,500
brutish

300
00:19:42,583 --> 00:19:43,416
-creatures.
-Hm.

301
00:19:43,500 --> 00:19:45,375
No! I don't want to depend on humans!

302
00:19:46,375 --> 00:19:47,208
Ay…

303
00:19:47,291 --> 00:19:51,041
if only we were able to cross over to the
Realm of Existence…

304
00:19:51,541 --> 00:19:53,416
this would be a different story.

305
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:55,666
And… is there…

306
00:19:55,750 --> 00:19:56,958
anyone who can cross over?

307
00:19:57,041 --> 00:19:58,333
In an age long forgotten,

308
00:19:58,416 --> 00:20:00,125
a very long time ago,

309
00:20:00,625 --> 00:20:03,250
{\an8}Fear of fear itself found its form.

310
00:20:03,750 --> 00:20:06,916
{\an8}And a colossal feathered spider was born:

311
00:20:07,416 --> 00:20:10,208
The magnificent Enkara.

312
00:20:11,625 --> 00:20:15,583
{\an8}Enkara realized her life was tethered to
the fear she awakened in the hearts of

313
00:20:15,666 --> 00:20:16,541
{\an8}humans.

314
00:20:18,666 --> 00:20:23,000
She used the Harpspider to cross and
thus subjugate the humans.

315
00:20:23,500 --> 00:20:25,625
Then the impertinent Ceimut

316
00:20:25,708 --> 00:20:27,625
defended humankind

317
00:20:27,708 --> 00:20:29,083
and challenged Enkara

318
00:20:29,166 --> 00:20:30,625
{\an8}to a mighty battle.

319
00:20:31,125 --> 00:20:33,333
{\an8}But Enkara captured Ceimut

320
00:20:33,416 --> 00:20:34,541
and devoured him.

321
00:20:34,625 --> 00:20:36,791
Using his fangs and his spines,

322
00:20:36,875 --> 00:20:40,000
-Ceimut tore Enkara's throat open
-Ahh!

323
00:20:40,500 --> 00:20:41,416
And escaped.

324
00:20:41,500 --> 00:20:42,791
Enkara was no more

325
00:20:43,291 --> 00:20:44,625
and from her remains

326
00:20:44,708 --> 00:20:46,833
two new species came into being:

327
00:20:47,333 --> 00:20:48,666
From her feathers…

328
00:20:49,166 --> 00:20:50,375
Tecothians, just like me!

329
00:20:50,458 --> 00:20:51,875
Yes, that's right!

330
00:20:51,958 --> 00:20:53,708
And from Enkara's silken webs,

331
00:20:53,791 --> 00:20:56,791
the Aradithians, like me, were born.

332
00:20:57,333 --> 00:21:01,083
{\an8}Yet in these days we don't have enough
power to materialize in the Realm of

333
00:21:01,166 --> 00:21:02,416
{\an8}Existence.

334
00:21:04,333 --> 00:21:05,541
{\an8}Ah, but I just…

335
00:21:05,625 --> 00:21:06,500
Mh,

336
00:21:06,583 --> 00:21:08,208
-You have just what, my Lord?
-uh…

337
00:21:08,291 --> 00:21:11,791
Uhm… I have just… remembered… that I'm
a little tired.

338
00:21:11,875 --> 00:21:12,708
Hm.

339
00:21:14,125 --> 00:21:16,458
Of course, of course, Your Highness!

340
00:21:17,166 --> 00:21:21,000
How foolish of me to trouble you
with such grown-up matters.

341
00:21:21,083 --> 00:21:23,250
Uh… I extend to you a cordial,

342
00:21:23,333 --> 00:21:26,125
genuine, and most deeply sincere apology.

343
00:21:26,666 --> 00:21:30,000
May you have the sweetest of nightmares.

344
00:21:32,083 --> 00:21:32,916
Thank you.

345
00:21:33,916 --> 00:21:34,750
Mh…

346
00:21:36,791 --> 00:21:37,625
Eww!

347
00:21:37,708 --> 00:21:39,916
Old socks are the worst in the entire
world!

348
00:21:41,541 --> 00:21:42,541
Just gross!

349
00:21:42,625 --> 00:21:44,833
Stop whining, Francisca Imelda,

350
00:21:44,916 --> 00:21:46,583
-Hm…
-as women,

351
00:21:46,666 --> 00:21:48,208
this has to be our duty.

352
00:21:48,291 --> 00:21:50,541
What I really want is to be a writer!

353
00:21:50,625 --> 00:21:52,958
I'll write about the being I saw
last night!

354
00:21:53,041 --> 00:21:54,791
Those terror stories of yours.

355
00:21:56,541 --> 00:21:59,458
That's it! A terror is what I saw!

356
00:21:59,541 --> 00:22:02,375
Stop with this nonsense!
You have a wild imagination,

357
00:22:02,875 --> 00:22:04,583
but you'll grow out of it.

358
00:22:17,416 --> 00:22:18,541
-Ah…
-They have even…

359
00:22:19,041 --> 00:22:20,250
{\an8}spoken of…

360
00:22:20,750 --> 00:22:24,000
-crossing over to the Realm of Existence.
-Huh?

361
00:22:24,083 --> 00:22:25,916
The two realms must always remain
separate,

362
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:27,875
How? Mh.

363
00:22:27,958 --> 00:22:30,500
Why can't they understand that
without that balance,

364
00:22:30,583 --> 00:22:32,083
we simply would not exist?

365
00:22:32,583 --> 00:22:33,416
I understand,

366
00:22:33,500 --> 00:22:35,625
but they have been giving too much heed
to

367
00:22:36,500 --> 00:22:37,333
Procustes.

368
00:22:37,416 --> 00:22:40,083
I know he's been by your side for an
entire era, but…

369
00:22:41,500 --> 00:22:43,250
have you considered…

370
00:22:43,333 --> 00:22:44,208
getting rid of him?

371
00:22:44,291 --> 00:22:46,291
{\an8}-Huh?
-No, no, no, no, no.

372
00:22:46,791 --> 00:22:49,541
Declaring war would only make
the situation worse.

373
00:22:50,041 --> 00:22:53,291
His ability as a Nightmare Maker
to travel with his consciousness

374
00:22:53,791 --> 00:22:55,500
has become too dangerous.

375
00:22:56,125 --> 00:22:58,333
-I'd rather keep him under close watch.
-Oh…

376
00:23:00,625 --> 00:23:02,666
Oh… my dear Saymut,

377
00:23:03,458 --> 00:23:06,541
I know you risk a great deal in bringing
me this message.

378
00:23:08,125 --> 00:23:10,083
You have proven yourself a true friend.

379
00:23:10,166 --> 00:23:11,666
I'll think on what to do.

380
00:23:11,750 --> 00:23:15,625
Don't take too long Ficturo, the Chiefs
are growing impatient,

381
00:23:15,708 --> 00:23:17,708
they won't stand idly by

382
00:23:18,208 --> 00:23:20,291
as all their clans fade away.

383
00:23:20,791 --> 00:23:23,625
I truly appreciate your advice, my old
friend.

384
00:23:26,375 --> 00:23:28,250
The Topus Terrentus…

385
00:23:28,875 --> 00:23:30,541
is in grave danger.

386
00:23:57,375 --> 00:24:02,041
{\an8}10 YEARS LATER

387
00:24:14,958 --> 00:24:17,208
Thank you for joining me, Mythelitas.

388
00:24:17,291 --> 00:24:18,583
I needed to clear my head.

389
00:24:18,666 --> 00:24:19,791
I'm… at your service.

390
00:24:20,291 --> 00:24:22,583
I'm concerned about our realm, there's…

391
00:24:23,166 --> 00:24:24,000
nothing I can do.

392
00:24:24,083 --> 00:24:26,541
It's none of my business, Your Highness,
but…

393
00:24:26,625 --> 00:24:30,291
have you taken a look at the Royal
Nightmare Maker's latest stories?

394
00:24:33,458 --> 00:24:35,125
Ah! Prince Herneval!

395
00:24:35,208 --> 00:24:36,041
No.

396
00:24:36,125 --> 00:24:38,708
Tell me why has the royal family
abandoned us?

397
00:24:38,791 --> 00:24:41,333
Why won't you act to prevent our demise?

398
00:24:41,416 --> 00:24:43,916
Long live Procuestes!

399
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:48,250
The only noble terror who truly
cares about us!

400
00:24:49,041 --> 00:24:51,125
Ah! Agh!

401
00:24:51,708 --> 00:24:53,791
No! No! Please don't!

402
00:24:53,875 --> 00:24:56,000
We will all slowly fade away.

403
00:24:56,875 --> 00:24:58,708
Uh… uh… What do I do?

404
00:24:58,791 --> 00:24:59,625
Ah-

405
00:25:00,458 --> 00:25:01,291
No…

406
00:25:03,958 --> 00:25:04,791
No!

407
00:25:20,791 --> 00:25:22,041
We need to make a change.

408
00:25:36,791 --> 00:25:37,625
No!

409
00:25:37,708 --> 00:25:39,000
My stories!

410
00:25:40,125 --> 00:25:42,041
I thought I told you that little girls

411
00:25:42,125 --> 00:25:43,750
cannot be writers.

412
00:26:01,416 --> 00:26:03,458
Today is the day, my dear terrors,

413
00:26:03,541 --> 00:26:06,250
the world is finally going to meet you.

414
00:26:14,625 --> 00:26:15,458
Ah…

415
00:26:33,375 --> 00:26:35,083
I implore you, Your Majesty…

416
00:26:35,166 --> 00:26:37,333
uh… I must insist one more time.

417
00:26:40,625 --> 00:26:41,458
Ficturo… don't!

418
00:26:53,791 --> 00:26:54,625
Ah…

419
00:26:59,041 --> 00:27:00,791
If you would only allow me,

420
00:27:00,875 --> 00:27:02,333
I would do my very best

421
00:27:02,833 --> 00:27:06,666
to assemble the wisest terrors and
find a way to cross over.

422
00:27:07,166 --> 00:27:10,625
Uh… it's your responsibility as the royal
family to save us from the-

423
00:27:10,708 --> 00:27:11,708
That's enough, Procustes.

424
00:27:11,791 --> 00:27:13,458
-Oh!
-Now leave us.

425
00:27:14,875 --> 00:27:16,750
Guards, show Procustes the way out.

426
00:27:17,250 --> 00:27:18,291
Yes, sir.

427
00:27:19,291 --> 00:27:20,125
He's gone, Dad.

428
00:27:21,541 --> 00:27:22,375
Mh…

429
00:27:23,166 --> 00:27:24,541
Thank you, son.

430
00:27:27,125 --> 00:27:27,958
Mom?

431
00:27:29,833 --> 00:27:32,083
Oh, hi, my beautiful son.

432
00:27:34,750 --> 00:27:37,166
Herneval,
I think you're losing weight, son.

433
00:27:37,250 --> 00:27:39,083
Have you been eating correctly?

434
00:27:39,583 --> 00:27:41,083
Mom… I'm alright,

435
00:27:41,583 --> 00:27:42,750
what about you?

436
00:27:49,458 --> 00:27:50,291
Are you unwell?

437
00:27:50,375 --> 00:27:51,208
No.

438
00:27:53,333 --> 00:27:54,166
Bring them.

439
00:27:56,875 --> 00:27:58,750
I just need some nightmares,

440
00:27:58,833 --> 00:27:59,916
it's nothing.

441
00:28:01,125 --> 00:28:04,375
{\an8}CLASSIC NIGHTMARES VOLUME XIII
BY PROCUSTES

442
00:28:04,458 --> 00:28:05,291
{\an8}Let's see…

443
00:28:06,041 --> 00:28:09,250
For years, Procustes has failed in his
promise of a masterpiece.

444
00:28:14,416 --> 00:28:15,250
Ah.

445
00:28:19,500 --> 00:28:20,333
Ah.

446
00:28:26,541 --> 00:28:27,958
{\an8}What do we have here…?

447
00:28:29,083 --> 00:28:29,916
Ow!

448
00:28:30,000 --> 00:28:34,791
Oh… the nightmares of today are not
what they once were.

449
00:28:39,666 --> 00:28:41,375
-Ow…
-Mom!

450
00:28:42,250 --> 00:28:44,250
Uh, no, please don't worry, honey.

451
00:28:44,916 --> 00:28:47,750
What matters above all is that you are
safe and well.

452
00:28:47,833 --> 00:28:50,333
No, but- how can you tell me not to
worry?

453
00:28:50,416 --> 00:28:54,083
Your mother and I have done everything we
could,

454
00:28:54,583 --> 00:28:58,458
-if only we had more time and strength…
-Mh.

455
00:29:00,625 --> 00:29:06,583
The time has come for you to make the
decisions for the Topus Terrentus.

456
00:29:07,083 --> 00:29:08,333
This is garbage!

457
00:29:10,208 --> 00:29:12,125
Don't underestimate Procustes.

458
00:29:12,708 --> 00:29:15,208
Each and every decision you make

459
00:29:15,291 --> 00:29:18,416
will have infinite consequences.

460
00:29:23,166 --> 00:29:24,875
{\an8}-Procustes!
-Ahh!

461
00:29:25,916 --> 00:29:26,833
Your Highness!

462
00:29:26,916 --> 00:29:27,875
Uh…

463
00:29:27,958 --> 00:29:29,708
I was right in the middle of my-

464
00:29:29,791 --> 00:29:30,750
uh… he he he…

465
00:29:30,833 --> 00:29:32,541
daily writing session.

466
00:29:32,625 --> 00:29:33,875
Doesn't look like it.

467
00:29:33,958 --> 00:29:36,625
Uh- uh…
well, you wouldn't understand this,

468
00:29:36,708 --> 00:29:37,541
but uh-

469
00:29:37,625 --> 00:29:40,458
it is vital that a writer have time
to himself,

470
00:29:40,541 --> 00:29:42,208
time for leisure and…

471
00:29:42,708 --> 00:29:43,583
and to do other…

472
00:29:43,666 --> 00:29:44,666
things.

473
00:29:44,750 --> 00:29:45,875
That's what concerns me.

474
00:29:45,958 --> 00:29:47,166
My parents are very sick.

475
00:29:47,250 --> 00:29:49,166
Of course, that is due to the fact that

476
00:29:49,250 --> 00:29:51,750
nowadays it's difficult to remain
healthy so…

477
00:29:51,833 --> 00:29:53,666
I think it's due to your stories.

478
00:29:53,750 --> 00:29:54,583
Uh, ahm.

479
00:29:54,666 --> 00:29:56,916
The nightmares you write no longer
frighten the humans.

480
00:29:57,000 --> 00:29:59,416
Ah. Because humans are all wrong!

481
00:29:59,500 --> 00:30:02,000
The people must always bear the blame!

482
00:30:03,541 --> 00:30:05,166
I want to bring in another writer,

483
00:30:05,250 --> 00:30:06,250
a human.

484
00:30:06,333 --> 00:30:08,750
That's blasphemy! That's nonsense!

485
00:30:08,833 --> 00:30:11,250
There can't be two Royal Nightmare
Makers!

486
00:30:11,750 --> 00:30:13,750
How could a human even hope to cross?

487
00:30:13,833 --> 00:30:15,958
I believe I've already figured it out.

488
00:30:16,958 --> 00:30:18,166
The time to change has come.

489
00:30:18,250 --> 00:30:21,625
As it happens, I am finishing my latest
masterpiece.

490
00:30:22,125 --> 00:30:24,458
Just be patient my young master.

491
00:30:24,541 --> 00:30:27,666
You'll witness the quality of my
nightmares.

492
00:30:29,875 --> 00:30:31,958
I've had enough patience and you know it.

493
00:30:35,791 --> 00:30:36,625
Ahh!

494
00:30:38,416 --> 00:30:39,708
He's a very holy man.

495
00:30:41,416 --> 00:30:43,708
And… he's been preaching for a long time.

496
00:30:45,250 --> 00:30:46,083
Francisca!

497
00:30:47,916 --> 00:30:49,500
-Hi there.
-Oh!

498
00:30:49,583 --> 00:30:50,666
Uh… Augusto!

499
00:30:51,333 --> 00:30:54,083
I'm on my way to see your father at his
editorial office.

500
00:30:54,166 --> 00:30:55,000
Yes, I know.

501
00:30:55,083 --> 00:30:57,791
I just wanted to wish you luck. Uh-
n- not that you need it, of course,

502
00:30:57,875 --> 00:31:00,791
the thing is- that my father can be an
expert in discouraging sometimes but-

503
00:31:00,875 --> 00:31:03,291
you'll do just fine.

504
00:31:03,375 --> 00:31:05,791
Alright, then… I'll go find out?

505
00:31:05,875 --> 00:31:06,791
Right, right.

506
00:31:07,333 --> 00:31:08,166
Sure.

507
00:31:08,666 --> 00:31:09,541
Mh… hm…

508
00:31:10,875 --> 00:31:11,958
Ehm… Alright…

509
00:31:12,458 --> 00:31:14,166
-good to see you.
-Of course.

510
00:31:14,250 --> 00:31:15,291
Oh!

511
00:31:15,375 --> 00:31:17,416
And uhm… uh- wha- wha- whatever happens,

512
00:31:17,500 --> 00:31:18,666
your stories have been…

513
00:31:19,291 --> 00:31:20,125
fascinating,

514
00:31:20,208 --> 00:31:21,250
since we were young.

515
00:31:25,708 --> 00:31:26,541
Ugh!

516
00:31:28,125 --> 00:31:30,375
My dear Miss Francisca Imelda,

517
00:31:30,875 --> 00:31:33,291
such a fine lady like you shouldn't be
writing

518
00:31:33,375 --> 00:31:34,375
these uh…

519
00:31:34,458 --> 00:31:36,041
horrible… stories.

520
00:31:36,625 --> 00:31:38,791
-Don't drag your good name in the mud.
-Uh…

521
00:31:39,916 --> 00:31:41,416
But did you at least read one?

522
00:31:41,500 --> 00:31:44,208
I would never waste my precious
time reading this…

523
00:31:44,291 --> 00:31:45,250
piece of trash!

524
00:31:46,125 --> 00:31:47,833
Art, literature,

525
00:31:48,333 --> 00:31:50,041
should emulate reality,

526
00:31:50,125 --> 00:31:51,208
not create

527
00:31:51,291 --> 00:31:52,333
a new one.

528
00:31:54,750 --> 00:31:55,583
-Wait! Oh…
-Uh…

529
00:32:08,708 --> 00:32:11,125
You were right all along, Grandma.

530
00:32:12,708 --> 00:32:13,541
