I want to help you.

1304
01:22:28,083 --> 01:22:29,250
And I know I can do it,

1305
01:22:29,333 --> 01:22:31,666
I have an idea that will do just the
trick.

1306
01:22:32,791 --> 01:22:34,041
Thank you, Frankelda but

1307
01:22:34,125 --> 01:22:35,375
I'm really not sure

1308
01:22:36,208 --> 01:22:37,916
all my plans have gone wrong,

1309
01:22:38,500 --> 01:22:39,333
I'm scared.

1310
01:22:39,833 --> 01:22:40,666
Ugh…

1311
01:22:41,333 --> 01:22:42,208
Well, I am not!

1312
01:22:42,291 --> 01:22:44,916
And I have to capture Procustes.

1313
01:22:45,458 --> 01:22:46,958
Sometimes I hate my reality,

1314
01:22:47,041 --> 01:22:50,125
but I understand that fiction wouldn't
exist without it!

1315
01:22:50,208 --> 01:22:53,666
If the barrier between realms falls,
all things will turn literal.

1316
01:22:54,166 --> 01:22:55,125
Ordinary.

1317
01:22:55,625 --> 01:22:57,166
No more imagination,

1318
01:22:57,250 --> 01:22:58,875
fascination or wonder.

1319
01:22:59,375 --> 01:23:01,041
Where do you plan to lock him up?

1320
01:23:02,541 --> 01:23:05,791
There's no stronger place than my
imagination.

1321
01:23:05,875 --> 01:23:07,791
What? Be careful, Frankelda!

1322
01:23:08,291 --> 01:23:11,041
I already made the mistake of
underestimating Procustes.

1323
01:23:11,125 --> 01:23:12,750
All my fears live there,

1324
01:23:13,458 --> 01:23:14,916
there's room for another.

1325
01:23:15,000 --> 01:23:16,875
No! You're risking too much.

1326
01:23:17,375 --> 01:23:18,708
It's not going to work!

1327
01:23:22,166 --> 01:23:25,625
I'm sure Procustes will force you to
send me one of his nightmares so

1328
01:23:25,708 --> 01:23:27,625
he can keep stealing my stories.

1329
01:23:27,708 --> 01:23:28,916
And when that happens,

1330
01:23:29,458 --> 01:23:31,000
the only thing you'll have to do

1331
01:23:31,083 --> 01:23:34,000
is send me one that I'll have written
myself, alright?

1332
01:23:34,791 --> 01:23:35,625
Trust in me.

1333
01:23:36,875 --> 01:23:37,750
Of course I do.

1334
01:23:54,666 --> 01:23:57,333
Uhm… There once was a kid named-

1335
01:23:57,416 --> 01:23:58,833
Bob! Eh- Bob.

1336
01:23:58,916 --> 01:24:00,875
Who… was hypnotized by

1337
01:24:00,958 --> 01:24:02,500
the… the Siren

1338
01:24:02,583 --> 01:24:04,333
and when he got to school

1339
01:24:05,125 --> 01:24:06,458
he wasn't wearing-

1340
01:24:06,541 --> 01:24:07,416
pants.

1341
01:24:07,500 --> 01:24:09,416
Ha, this is pure gold, of course.

1342
01:24:09,500 --> 01:24:11,541
I think I'd rather you didn't write
anything about me.

1343
01:24:11,625 --> 01:24:13,166
I told you earlier this is not
how writing works I need-

1344
01:24:13,250 --> 01:24:15,958
Even a human writes better than you.
You're a disgrace.

1345
01:24:16,041 --> 01:24:19,083
None of you have a place here in the
Topus Terrentus!

1346
01:24:32,875 --> 01:24:33,708
Oh…

1347
01:24:37,916 --> 01:24:38,750
Oh…

1348
01:24:40,500 --> 01:24:42,833
The King and Queen are hurt,

1349
01:24:42,916 --> 01:24:43,875
I have to-

1350
01:24:46,458 --> 01:24:47,291
Saymuth!

1351
01:24:48,083 --> 01:24:49,875
-Your Highness
-No!

1352
01:24:49,958 --> 01:24:51,083
Save your parents.

1353
01:24:51,708 --> 01:24:53,625
Save the Topus Terrentus.

1354
01:24:54,875 --> 01:24:56,041
I'm sorry.

1355
01:24:58,875 --> 01:25:00,250
Mythelitas!

1356
01:25:02,500 --> 01:25:04,250
Mythelitas, what are you doing?

1357
01:25:11,208 --> 01:25:12,041
Ah…

1358
01:25:14,791 --> 01:25:15,625
Ow!

1359
01:25:15,708 --> 01:25:17,833
-If either of you dares to move again…
-Ah…

1360
01:25:17,916 --> 01:25:20,250
the King and Queen are history.

1361
01:25:20,333 --> 01:25:22,000
I'm not fooling around!

1362
01:25:22,083 --> 01:25:23,250
Stop, Procustes!

1363
01:25:23,333 --> 01:25:24,875
I'll do whatever you want.

1364
01:25:28,208 --> 01:25:31,375
Is… your girlfriend going to cooperate?

1365
01:25:34,208 --> 01:25:35,750
How does it feel to have to steal stories

1366
01:25:35,833 --> 01:25:37,416
-from a human?
-Ugh…

1367
01:25:37,500 --> 01:25:38,416
Huh?

1368
01:25:38,500 --> 01:25:40,083
You're a pathetic joke.

1369
01:25:42,250 --> 01:25:43,083
-Oh…
-Sorry…

1370
01:25:44,541 --> 01:25:45,375
Heh…

1371
01:25:48,416 --> 01:25:52,291
Send her this nightmare where she'll
live until she's written

1372
01:25:52,791 --> 01:25:56,375
every single story I could ever need

1373
01:25:56,916 --> 01:26:01,250
I'm sure her imagination will be
stimulated given the recent events.

1374
01:26:01,333 --> 01:26:05,083
I will then consider releasing you,
depending on your good behavior, of

1375
01:26:05,166 --> 01:26:06,041
course.

1376
01:26:18,250 --> 01:26:19,083
Ow…

1377
01:26:25,250 --> 01:26:26,083
Ah!

1378
01:26:30,416 --> 01:26:34,291
This… may seem like the story of a naive
girl who would do anything to try to

1379
01:26:34,375 --> 01:26:36,750
escape her reality,

1380
01:26:37,750 --> 01:26:38,958
but it isn't…

1381
01:26:39,458 --> 01:26:40,875
What is this?

1382
01:26:40,958 --> 01:26:41,916
This…

1383
01:26:42,000 --> 01:26:43,125
is the story

1384
01:26:43,208 --> 01:26:46,708
of a human writer who faced her fears

1385
01:26:46,791 --> 01:26:51,041
and decided to write her own story!

1386
01:26:51,916 --> 01:26:52,750
Agh!

1387
01:26:55,833 --> 01:26:58,208
The Nightmare Maker thought he had the

1388
01:26:58,291 --> 01:27:00,708
-poor girl trapped in her worst nightmare,
-Ahh!

1389
01:27:00,791 --> 01:27:02,666
-Ow…
-But it was her who had him.

1390
01:27:03,166 --> 01:27:05,916
This is not the story I wrote!

1391
01:27:06,000 --> 01:27:09,166
He was so obsolete and useless that he
ended up turning into his own crumbling

1392
01:27:09,250 --> 01:27:10,958
-house.
-Oh…

1393
01:27:12,041 --> 01:27:14,791
And right before entering eternal rest,

1394
01:27:14,875 --> 01:27:17,125
he discovered that his worst nightmare

1395
01:27:17,208 --> 01:27:19,458
had only just come true.

1396
01:27:20,041 --> 01:27:22,000
He had been replaced.

1397
01:27:22,500 --> 01:27:25,166
His existence was meaningless.

1398
01:27:25,250 --> 01:27:30,208
He had gone down in history as the most
mediocre terror of all.

1399
01:27:30,708 --> 01:27:32,916
He… was just a sad memory

1400
01:27:33,416 --> 01:27:35,625
of another time of glory.

1401
01:27:38,583 --> 01:27:40,500
Yes! I knew it would work!

1402
01:27:43,541 --> 01:27:46,875
{\an8}This is definitely not the story I wrote!

1403
01:27:47,875 --> 01:27:49,041
Ahh! Help me!

1404
01:27:49,541 --> 01:27:50,375
Ah!

1405
01:27:54,000 --> 01:27:55,708
Procustes is changing the dream.

1406
01:27:57,791 --> 01:27:58,625
No!

1407
01:27:59,416 --> 01:28:00,375
Frankelda!

1408
01:28:01,208 --> 01:28:02,833
Stay away from her…

1409
01:28:03,625 --> 01:28:04,833
Those are…

1410
01:28:05,458 --> 01:28:07,250
Procustes's orders.

1411
01:28:07,333 --> 01:28:09,708
Please stop! Can't you see she needs help?

1412
01:28:09,791 --> 01:28:10,750
Frankelda, come back.

1413
01:28:10,833 --> 01:28:11,708
I said…

1414
01:28:12,625 --> 01:28:13,875
stay away!

1415
01:28:47,041 --> 01:28:47,875
Oh!

1416
01:28:48,666 --> 01:28:49,708
What happened to me?

1417
01:28:52,416 --> 01:28:53,250
Huh?

1418
01:28:54,500 --> 01:28:55,750
Frankelda.

1419
01:28:59,291 --> 01:29:00,791
Ah! Ah…

1420
01:29:01,541 --> 01:29:02,375
Frankelda,

1421
01:29:02,458 --> 01:29:03,791
this is your story,

1422
01:29:04,291 --> 01:29:05,416
not his.

1423
01:29:09,500 --> 01:29:10,333
Mhh…

1424
01:29:12,250 --> 01:29:13,541
Mh… mhh…

1425
01:29:17,291 --> 01:29:20,791
You think you're alone here.

1426
01:29:23,500 --> 01:29:27,250
That the nights belong to you,

1427
01:29:29,958 --> 01:29:33,083
but within the nightmares

1428
01:29:36,041 --> 01:29:40,166
don't trust what you can't prove.

1429
01:29:46,875 --> 01:29:50,625
It's my ink that stares at us.

1430
01:29:53,250 --> 01:29:57,000
-And my eyes rewrite you.
-Ah…

1431
01:29:59,541 --> 01:30:02,666
You dwell in the shadows.

1432
01:30:05,791 --> 01:30:10,541
In those pages you're hiding. And it's

1433
01:30:11,791 --> 01:30:17,750
-not so dreadful, You can see the unknown
-And it's not so dreadful, You can see the

1434
01:30:17,833 --> 01:30:23,875
-when you read through.
-unknown when you read through.

1435
01:30:24,500 --> 01:30:30,166
-This invisible ink that now lives
-This invisible ink that now lives

1436
01:30:30,250 --> 01:30:34,875
-without a breath,
-without a breath,

1437
01:30:36,500 --> 01:30:40,416
-an author who's…
-an author who's…

1438
01:30:41,208 --> 01:30:42,166
A terror!

1439
01:30:42,958 --> 01:30:44,666
Hm! Your tongue

1440
01:30:44,750 --> 01:30:47,291
-can no longer hurt me!
-Uh…

1441
01:30:47,375 --> 01:30:48,333
{\an8}But how

1442
01:30:48,416 --> 01:30:50,083
{\an8}piercing and cruel

1443
01:30:50,166 --> 01:30:51,916
{\an8}its words can be.

1444
01:30:53,958 --> 01:30:54,791
Huh?

1445
01:30:56,916 --> 01:30:58,625
-Frankelda!
-Oh…

1446
01:31:03,041 --> 01:31:03,875
Ahh!

1447
01:31:10,916 --> 01:31:12,958
-Now sleep!
-Ow…

1448
01:31:17,250 --> 01:31:20,958
You may claim victory this round…

1449
01:31:21,041 --> 01:31:26,666
but I shall not be trapped in here
by myself…

1450
01:31:26,750 --> 01:31:28,583
We need to find a way out!

1451
01:31:31,666 --> 01:31:33,000
I'm sorry Frankelda,

1452
01:31:33,083 --> 01:31:34,125
I failed again.

1453
01:31:35,291 --> 01:31:36,125
Herneval?

1454
01:31:36,625 --> 01:31:37,500
Herneval, what's wrong?

1455
01:31:37,583 --> 01:31:39,958
This is just a dream, no one can hurt
you here.

1456
01:31:40,458 --> 01:31:41,291
Not here, no…

1457
01:31:42,000 --> 01:31:43,708
But I was wounded in the palace,

1458
01:31:43,791 --> 01:31:45,375
before I came to get you.

1459
01:31:45,916 --> 01:31:47,416
What? No!

1460
01:31:48,083 --> 01:31:48,958
No! No!

1461
01:31:50,458 --> 01:31:52,708
-Mh.
-It is all my fault.

1462
01:31:54,750 --> 01:31:55,708
It's not your fault,

1463
01:31:55,791 --> 01:31:57,458
you saved my parents.

1464
01:31:58,000 --> 01:32:00,500
Herneval, you are the only one that
matters to me.

1465
01:32:00,583 --> 01:32:03,041
You must find a way out of here.

1466
01:32:03,625 --> 01:32:05,125
You're going to be alright.

1467
01:32:11,041 --> 01:32:13,875
{\an8}Our story was the first one I started
writing.

1468
01:32:13,958 --> 01:32:18,166
Thanks to you I got to know this place
I had always dreamed of visiting.

1469
01:32:18,250 --> 01:32:20,583
Thanks to you I got to know myself.

1470
01:32:20,666 --> 01:32:23,625
Our story cannot die because stories…

1471
01:32:23,708 --> 01:32:25,083
are immortal.

1472
01:32:25,583 --> 01:32:27,125
You live right here.

1473
01:32:42,083 --> 01:32:42,916
Huh?

1474
01:32:53,083 --> 01:32:53,916
Mh…

1475
01:33:03,625 --> 01:33:04,458
{\an8}Ah…

1476
01:33:07,333 --> 01:33:08,166
Ah.

1477
01:33:37,333 --> 01:33:38,166
Ahh…

1478
01:33:39,458 --> 01:33:40,333
What have I done?

1479
01:33:41,958 --> 01:33:42,791
No!

1480
01:33:48,041 --> 01:33:49,875
I thought it was a nightmare,

1481
01:33:50,708 --> 01:33:51,541
please.

1482
01:33:52,333 --> 01:33:54,958
Wake up, please, wake up, Herneval.

1483
01:33:55,041 --> 01:33:56,166
Please don't leave us.

1484
01:34:07,208 --> 01:34:08,041
Ah…

1485
01:34:09,333 --> 01:34:10,416
-Lady Coyote!
-Ah…

1486
01:34:11,250 --> 01:34:12,083
Hm.

1487
01:34:12,166 --> 01:34:15,000
{\an8}I knew you would never conspire
against us.

1488
01:34:16,583 --> 01:34:17,416
No!

1489
01:34:20,541 --> 01:34:21,416
My son!

1490
01:34:24,041 --> 01:34:25,666
Please, Lady Coyote,

1491
01:34:26,166 --> 01:34:28,291
is there anything you can do for them?

1492
01:34:33,333 --> 01:34:35,833
There is nothing to be done.

1493
01:34:47,708 --> 01:34:48,750
Your Majesties,

1494
01:34:49,666 --> 01:34:51,541
I cannot live with this dishonor.

1495
01:34:52,750 --> 01:34:54,375
{\an8}I ask that my punishment

1496
01:34:55,666 --> 01:34:58,083
{\an8}be to pay with my own life.

1497
01:34:58,625 --> 01:34:59,833
No, Mythelitas.

1498
01:35:01,083 --> 01:35:02,583
{\an8}You carry a great burden,

1499
01:35:02,666 --> 01:35:04,250
{\an8}but you're not to blame.

1500
01:35:04,333 --> 01:35:06,291
{\an8}You are like a son to us.

1501
01:35:06,375 --> 01:35:09,083
{\an8}We don't know where Ceimuth
sent the traitors,

1502
01:35:09,666 --> 01:35:12,708
{\an8}but we must ensure that they cannot do
any more harm.

1503
01:35:13,208 --> 01:35:17,166
Find them all and bring them before us.

1504
01:35:17,250 --> 01:35:19,000
Beware, Mythelitas,

1505
01:35:19,083 --> 01:35:21,416
a great war between the Seven Clans

1506
01:35:21,916 --> 01:35:23,625
is about to begin.

1507
01:35:23,708 --> 01:35:24,708
I swear,

1508
01:35:25,625 --> 01:35:27,333
by Prince Herneval,

1509
01:35:28,333 --> 01:35:29,416
not to rest

1510
01:35:30,333 --> 01:35:32,083
until the last traitor

1511
01:35:33,250 --> 01:35:34,083
falls!

1512
01:35:41,458 --> 01:35:42,625
Tecothians!

1513
01:35:43,291 --> 01:35:46,541
For the Prince of Terrors!

1514
01:35:59,333 --> 01:36:00,541
Thank you, Frankelda,

1515
01:36:01,041 --> 01:36:03,125
I know this is not exactly

1516
01:36:03,208 --> 01:36:04,666
what you wanted.

1517
01:36:05,208 --> 01:36:06,416
But all humans

1518
01:36:06,916 --> 01:36:08,666
will know your stories.

1519
01:36:20,250 --> 01:36:21,708
Please… come back.

1520
01:36:37,166 --> 01:36:38,000
I am…

1521
01:36:39,000 --> 01:36:39,833
alive!

1522
01:36:41,750 --> 01:36:42,583
Where are you?

1523
01:36:43,708 --> 01:36:44,541
Where are you?

1524
01:36:45,666 --> 01:36:47,500
Frankelda, where are you?

1525
01:36:51,583 --> 01:36:53,000
-Ah!
-Ahh!

1526
01:36:53,083 --> 01:36:53,916
{\an8}Ah…

1527
01:36:54,000 --> 01:36:54,833
Hello.

1528
01:36:55,458 --> 01:36:56,791
Huh? Who exactly…

1529
01:36:57,291 --> 01:36:58,250
are you?

1530
01:36:58,333 --> 01:36:59,625
Who do you think?

1531
01:37:06,875 --> 01:37:07,875
{\an8}Amazing!

1532
01:37:08,541 --> 01:37:10,208
-Are you…?
-I am…

1533
01:37:10,291 --> 01:37:11,833
You are… truth!

1534
01:37:12,458 --> 01:37:14,125
-And fiction…
-We still exist!

1535
01:37:14,208 --> 01:37:17,666
Ah… As long as you tell our story,

1536
01:37:17,750 --> 01:37:19,250
-we'll keep existing.
-Uh…

1537
01:37:19,333 --> 01:37:20,791
{\an8}Herneval, I love you!

1538
01:37:21,333 --> 01:37:22,208
{\an8}I love you!

1539
01:37:22,708 --> 01:37:24,666
{\an8}I love you too, Frankelda.

1540
01:37:25,166 --> 01:37:27,291
{\an8}And I don't really care what form I take

1541
01:37:27,375 --> 01:37:29,708
as long as I can spend an eternity
with you.

1542
01:37:29,791 --> 01:37:30,625
Wait, what?

1543
01:37:31,583 --> 01:37:33,666
An… eternity like this?

1544
01:37:34,166 --> 01:37:35,666
That is all up to you now…

1545
01:37:35,750 --> 01:37:38,125
Up to me? Is it up to me after

1546
01:37:38,208 --> 01:37:39,791
everything we've been through?

1547
01:37:39,875 --> 01:37:41,333
{\an8}Of course you are the writer.

1548
01:37:41,416 --> 01:37:43,458
Well- I'm the writer of a

1549
01:37:43,541 --> 01:37:44,666
sad story.

1550
01:37:45,166 --> 01:37:46,916
Do you really feel that way?

1551
01:37:47,000 --> 01:37:47,958
Well, yes!

1552
01:37:48,708 --> 01:37:50,250
But… sadness can…

1553
01:37:50,750 --> 01:37:53,166
come in different forms and shades.

1554
01:37:53,666 --> 01:37:56,750
A hundred authors can write the
same event

1555
01:37:56,833 --> 01:37:59,458
and create a hundred different stories.

1556
01:38:00,208 --> 01:38:02,250
Is this how your story ends, Frankelda?

1557
01:38:02,333 --> 01:38:06,125
I refuse to let this be how our
story ends.

1558
01:38:07,291 --> 01:38:09,541
I don't care how bitter my situation is,

1559
01:38:10,041 --> 01:38:12,583
or how long my soul has endured
confinement,

1560
01:38:13,083 --> 01:38:16,083
because I am the master of my destiny!

1561
01:38:16,583 --> 01:38:20,333
I am the writer of my own life!

1562
01:38:24,125 --> 01:38:25,125
Then write me!

1563
01:38:26,041 --> 01:38:27,916
Let's live one more time!

1564
01:38:28,000 --> 01:38:28,958
Yes!

1565
01:38:32,625 --> 01:38:33,458
{\an8}This…

1566
01:38:33,541 --> 01:38:36,125
{\an8}is the story of two realms so utterly
different, that they could resemble

1567
01:38:36,208 --> 01:38:38,416
each other. Two realms that do not
even exist for the numb consciousnesses.

1568
01:38:38,500 --> 01:38:40,375
Two realms so utterly different,
